node_modules/
three-0.160.0/
three-0.169.0/
shots/
# candidates/* not candidates/ — git refuses to re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded by a directory pattern, so the negation below is dead
# unless the contents are what's excluded.
candidates/*
# The manifest saying which captured frame was promoted IS tracked. Four lines of
# JSON, and the only record of why assets/previews/ looks the way it does; without
# it a future session has to re-choose all seven from scratch.
!candidates/chosen.json

# package-lock.json IS tracked (locked decision #52) — node_modules/ above stays
# ignored (locked decision #12, dev-only tooling), but an unpinned lockfile meant
# every session's `npm install` floated on whatever the registry served that day,
# with no diff to point at when a dependency's behavior changed underneath
# everyone. That's exactly how the puppeteer-core waitForFunction break (round
# 2) went unnoticed until three separate threads hit it independently.
